Subject: [PATCH 1/3] rmi4d: discover the DT touch node and wait on its
 attention IRQ

rmi4d mapped GENI MMIO before common::init and panicked at start on
qemu-oneplus6. It now initialises the memory root first, finds the enabled
syna,rmi4-i2c node under its qcom,geni-i2c bus in /scheme/kernel.dtb,
claims the interrupts-extended attention IRQ through the irq scheme and
reads the touch controller only when that IRQ fires (one drain read after
arming). Pointer events come from a host-tested Tracker. geni-i2cd gets
the same common::init fix and the base-addressed mapping.

